# Test: a peer created from a dynamic group is subject to the group's import
# filter chain, and the chain DECIDES: it accepts one route and rejects another.
#
# VALIDATES: the bgp-level and group-level `filter import` chains reach a dynamic
#            member (peersAndDynamicGroups, internal/component/bgp/config/peers.go),
#            and the decision runs for that member
#            (handleFilterUpdate, internal/component/bgp/plugins/filter_prefix).
# PREVENTS: an IXP route server that applies NO policy to its members. Until
#           2026-08-13 the dynamic groups were built by a walk of their own, and
#           no `ImportFilters` assignment was reachable from it: every member got
#           an empty chain. No prefix filtering, no AS-path filtering, no
#           community handling, no IRR validation, on the one peer population an
#           operator has not vetted by hand. The config named a policy, `ze config
#           validate` accepted it, and nothing enforced it.
#
# DISCRIMINATION: under the defect NEITHER decision line exists, because the chain
# was empty and the filter plugin was never dispatched to. The route would have
# been installed instead. The two lines also discriminate against each other: a
# chain that rejected everything (a filter dispatched with the wrong name fails
# closed) would lose the accept line, and a chain that accepted everything would
# lose the reject line. Measured on 2026-08-13 by deleting the dynamic branch of
# the filter-chain assignment in peers.go: both `prefix-list` lines disappear.
#
# The peer takes the ACTIVE role and dials ze (--dial): the group is `ip dynamic`
# + `connect false`, so ze only ever ACCEPTS. No static peer is configured, so the
# only socket is the one the group asks for and the only peer is the one the
# inbound connection creates.

# "dynamic peer created" is an Info line and the daemon's base level is warn
# (ze.log, internal/core/slogutil/slogutil.go). The filter plugin's decision
# lines are Info on their own subsystem.
option=env:var=ze.log.bgp.reactor:value=info
option=env:var=ze.log.bgp.filter.prefix:value=info

stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=asn:value=65001
option=tcp_connections:value=1

# ONE UPDATE carrying TWO prefixes, so one filter decision covers both and the
# assertion cannot be satisfied by a batching accident. ORIGIN=IGP,
# AS_PATH=[65001], NEXT_HOP=1.1.1.1, then:
#
#   10.0.0.0/24  (18 0A0000)  matches entry 10.0.0.0/8 ge 16 le 24 -> accept
#   192.0.2.0/24 (18 C00002)  matches no entry                     -> implicit deny
action=send:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF003302000000144001010040020602010000FDE940030401010101180A000018C00002
EOF_PEER

# One dynamic group and nothing else: the route-server shape. The import chain is
# stated at the group level, which is where an IXP states its member policy.
# tmpfs rather than stdin because the runner writes daemon.pid and daemon.ready
# beside the config, and the compiled trigger waits on both.
tmpfs=ze-bgp.conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	policy {
		prefix-list CUSTOMERS {
			entry 10.0.0.0/8 {
				ge 16
				le 24
				action accept
			}
		}
	}

	group ix {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip dynamic
				connect false
				range 127.0.0.0/8
			}
			local {
				ip 127.0.0.1
				accept true
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
			family {
				ipv4/unicast {
					mode enable
					prefix {
						maximum 10000
					}
				}
			}
			capability {
				graceful-restart disable
			}
		}
		filter {
			import [ bgp-filter-prefix:CUSTOMERS ]
		}
		behavior {
			group-updates disable
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

# Trigger: let the session establish and both UPDATEs drain, then stop the
# daemon. The sleep only has to cover a dial the peer retries every 500ms against
# a daemon that has already written daemon.ready; too short and the file fails on
# a missing decision line rather than passing quietly.

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --dial 127.0.0.1:$PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=background:seq=2:exec=ze-test fixture plugin/dynamic-peer-applies-group-filters-trigger
cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze --plugin ze.bgp-filter-prefix --plugin ze.bgp-adj-rib-in start ze-bgp.conf:timeout=30s

# The session above really was a DYNAMIC peer's. Without this the decision lines
# would hold for any peer ze accepted.
expect=stderr:contains=dynamic peer created

# ... and it reached Established, so the UPDATEs were carried by a live session.
expect=stderr:contains=session established

# The group's chain ran for that member, and it DISCRIMINATED: one prefix of the
# UPDATE accepted, the other rejected, so the engine rewrites the NLRI to the
# accepted subset (applyFilterDelta). The line names the list, so a dispatch to
# another filter would not satisfy it, and it names both counts, so a chain that
# accepted everything or rejected everything would not either.
expect=stderr:pattern=prefix-list modify.*filter=CUSTOMERS.*accepted=1 rejected=1
expect=stderr:pattern=nlri="ipv4/unicast add 10\.0\.0\.0/24 192\.0\.2\.0/24"
